<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
{{#unless is_terminal}}<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="10">{{/unless}}
<title>Pay with Monero</title>
{{> styles}}
<style>
/* This page is meant to be embedded in a merchant's own checkout flow via
   iframe - deliberately no site nav partial included, no top bar, nothing
   that reads as "you've left the merchant's site". It also carries
   *no script element at all* - a real customer paying real money must be able
   to trust and use this page with JavaScript disabled; a `<meta
   http-equiv="refresh">` above re-fetches the whole page every 10s while
   the order is still in progress (stopped once `is_terminal`, same as the
   old poll loop's own "stop once done" rule), and every value below
   (status, amounts, the progress bar's fill, the relative "expires in"
   time, even the expiry pill's own color) is already correct in the HTML
   this response returns - see `http::checkout::checkout_page` and
   `templates::format_duration_until`.
   Reuses the same tokens `_styles.html.hbs` defines (monospace, hard
   borders, the one accent color) so it never reads as a foreign,
   third-party-widget-looking thing dropped into a merchant's page - but
   deliberately just ONE bordered surface for the whole widget, not a card
   nested inside another card: stacking a border around every sub-section
   the way an earlier version of this page did reads as a picture-in-
   picture video call, not a payment screen.

   Layout: single column under ~700px (a merchant's own narrow widget embed,
   or a phone), a two-column "QR+amount+address" / "progress+refund+history"
   split above it (this page's own `checkout_share.html.hbs` wrapper, and any
   merchant embedding it at real desktop width) - real crypto-checkout pages
   researched while building this (BTCPay Server, OpenNode, general
   crypto-checkout UX guidance) consistently: use the QR code at >=200px, put
   an explicit copy affordance right next to the address rather than relying
   on the customer to already know to select-all a readonly field, and keep
   the expiry timer low-key (a quiet color shift, not a big red countdown)
   rather than anxiety-inducing. */
body { padding: 1.2rem; background: var(--paper-raised); }
.pay-wrap { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }
.pay-header { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.6em; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 0.8em; }
.status-pending, .status-unconfirmed, .status-confirming, .status-partial { background: var(--tint-warning); }
.status-paid { background: var(--tint-success); }
.status-expired, .status-unknown { background: var(--tint-error); }
/* Quiet by design (see this style block's own header comment) - a plain
   bordered pill in the muted tone until time actually starts running low,
   then a two-stage color shift (`expiry_urgency_class`, picked server-side
   in `http::checkout::render_checkout_page`) rather than one alarming red
   the whole time. */
.expiry-pill {
  display: inline-block;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  color: var(--muted);
  padding: 0.05em 0.6em;
  font-size: 0.8em;
  font-weight: 700;
}
.expiry-pill.expiry-soon { border-color: var(--warning); color: var(--warning); background: var(--tint-warning); }
.expiry-pill.expiry-urgent { border-color: var(--error); color: var(--error); background: var(--tint-error); }
.pay-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; text-align: center; }
@media (min-width: 700px) {
  .pay-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 300px) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2rem; text-align: left; }
  .pay-col-primary { text-align: center; }
  .pay-header { justify-content: space-between; }
}
.amount { font-size: 2.2rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0.2em 0 0.1em; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
.fiat-amount { color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 1.2em; }
.qr-wrap { margin: 0 auto 1.2em; display: flex; justify-content: center; }
.qr-wrap svg { width: 208px; height: 208px; }
/* The address itself: a `<textarea readonly>` wrapped in its own `<label>`
   (real HTML behavior - clicking anywhere in a `<label>` associated with a
   form control focuses it, no JS needed) so the whole card is one large,
   obviously-tappable target, not just the thin text box - a long-press on
   mobile or a click-drag/triple-click on desktop still needs no JavaScript
   at all to actually select-and-copy from there. A visible "copy" glyph and
   `:focus-within` highlight give real, immediate visual feedback that
   something happened when tapped, even though the actual clipboard write
   still has to be the browser's own native select+copy - this page carries
   no script element to do that step automatically (see this style block's own
   header comment for why that's a hard rule here, not an oversight). */
.address-card {
  display: block;
  text-align: left;
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  background: var(--paper-raised);
  padding: 0.6em 0.7em;
  cursor: pointer;
  margin: 0 0 1.4em;
}
.address-card:focus-within { outline: 3px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 0; }
.address-card-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5em; }
.address-copy-icon { flex: none; width: 1.1em; height: 1.1em; color: var(--muted); }
.address-label { display: block; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.8em; margin: 0 0 0.35em; }
.address-text {
  flex: 1;
  width: 100%;
  font-size: 0.85em;
  resize: none;
  border: none;
  background: none;
  padding: 0;
  height: 2.6em;
  cursor: pointer;
}
.section {
  text-align: left;
  margin-top: 1.6em;
  padding-top: 1.4em;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
}
.pay-grid > .pay-col-primary > .section:first-child,
.pay-grid > .pay-col-secondary > .section:first-child { margin-top: 0; padding-top: 0; border-top: none; }
.progress-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 0.85em; margin-bottom: 0.4em; }
.progress-bar { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); overflow: hidden; height: 0.5em; background: var(--paper); }
.progress-fill { height: 100%; background: var(--accent); }
.payments-table { font-size: 0.8em; margin-top: 1.2em; }
.meta { margin-top: 1.4em; font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--muted); text-align: left; }
.visually-hidden {
  position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; padding: 0; margin: -1px;
  overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0,0,0,0); white-space: nowrap; border: 0;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="pay-wrap">

<h1 class="visually-hidden">Monero payment of {{xmr_amount}} XMR</h1>

<div class="pay-header">
<span id="status-badge" class="tag {{status_class}}">{{status_label}}</span>
{{#unless is_terminal}}<span class="expiry-pill {{expiry_urgency_class}}">Expires in {{expires_in_display}}</span>{{/unless}}
</div>

{{#if double_spend_detected_at}}
<div id="double-spend-banner" class="error" role="alert">
A payment toward this order was reversed by a blockchain double-spend, detected at
<span id="double-spend-time">{{{double_spend_detected_at_display}}}</span>.
{{#unless is_terminal}}This order's status above reflects only still-valid payments.{{/unless}}
</div>
{{/if}}

<div class="pay-grid">
<div class="pay-col-primary">

<span class="visually-hidden" id="amount-label">Amount due</span>
<div class="amount" id="xmr-amount" aria-labelledby="amount-label">{{xmr_amount}} XMR</div>
<div class="fiat-amount">&asymp; {{amount}} {{currency}}</div>

<!-- The QR code is redundant with the copyable address text right below it,
     so it's hidden from assistive tech (qr_svg_for_html stamps
     role="presentation" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" onto the SVG
     itself) rather than announced as an unlabeled image. -->
<div class="qr-wrap">{{{qr_code_svg}}}</div>

<label class="address-card" for="address">
<span class="address-label" id="address-label">Send exactly this amount to - tap to select, then copy</span>
<span class="address-card-row">
<svg class="address-copy-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="9" y="9" width="12" height="12" rx="1"></rect><path d="M5 15H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h10a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v1"></path></svg>
<textarea class="address-text" id="address" readonly aria-labelledby="address-label">{{address}}</textarea>
</span>
</label>

</div>
<div class="pay-col-secondary">

<div class="section">
<div class="progress-row">
<span id="confirmations-label">{{confirmations}} / {{confirmations_required}} confirmations</span>
<span id="received-label">{{amount_received_xmr}} XMR received</span>
</div>
<div class="progress-bar" id="progress-bar" role="progressbar" aria-labelledby="confirmations-label"
     aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="{{confirmations_required}}" aria-valuenow="{{confirmations}}"
     aria-valuetext="{{confirmations}} of {{confirmations_required}} confirmations">
<div class="progress-fill" id="progress-fill" style="width: {{progress_percent}}%"></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section">
{{#if refund_address}}
<span class="address-label" id="refund-address-label">Refund address on file</span>
<textarea class="address-text" id="refund-address" readonly aria-labelledby="refund-address-label" style="border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 0.6em; height: 3.4em;">{{refund_address}}</textarea>
{{else}}
<form method="post" action="/pay/{{pk}}/orders/{{payment_id}}/refund-address">
<label for="refund_address">Refund address <span class="field-help" style="display:inline">(optional)</span></label>
{{#if refund_address_error}}<div class="error">{{refund_address_error}}</div>{{/if}}
<input type="text" id="refund_address" name="refund_address" placeholder="Your Monero refund address">
<span class="field-help">If this order is ever overpaid, expires with funds already sent, or otherwise needs a
refund, we'll send it back to this address - not to the address above. Only you can set this; the merchant
never sees or chooses it.</span>
<button type="submit" class="btn-secondary">Save</button>
</form>
{{/if}}
</div>

{{#if payments}}
<div class="section">
<table class="payments-table">
<caption class="visually-hidden">Individual payments received toward this order</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Tx</th><th scope="col">Amount</th><th scope="col">Confirmations</th></tr></thead>
<tbody id="payments-body">
{{#each payments}}
<tr>
<td>{{this.txid_short}}</td>
<td>{{this.amount_xmr}} XMR</td>
<td>{{#if this.is_zero_conf}}mempool{{else}}{{this.confirmations}}{{/if}}</td>
</tr>
{{/each}}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{{/if}}

<div class="meta">
Payment ID: {{payment_id}}<br>
{{#unless is_terminal}}Expires in {{expires_in_display}}{{/unless}}
</div>

</div>
</div>

</div>
</body>
</html>
